%%{init: {"theme": "base", "themeVariables": {"fontSize": "15px", "actorBkg": "#eef2ff", "actorBorder": "#6366f1", "actorTextColor": "#1e1b4b", "noteBkgColor": "#f1f5f9", "noteBorderColor": "#94a3b8", "loopTextColor": "#334155", "labelBoxBkgColor": "#f1f5f9", "labelBoxBorderColor": "#94a3b8", "signalColor": "#475569", "signalTextColor": "#0f172a"}, "sequence": {"mirrorActors": false, "noteMargin": 12}}}%%
%% One question: how an answer gets accepted and collected.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant R as Runner (host)
    participant S as Sandbox (pi agent)
    participant M as Model · via LiteLLM

    Note over R: skip if this question already<br/>has an ok or empty record
    R->>S: docker run: pages, text layer, prompt
    S->>M: prompt + page images + tool list

    loop until accepted, plain-text reply, or 25 turns
        M-->>S: tool call
        alt zoom / bash / read / write
            S->>S: run tool
            S->>M: tool result (crop image or output)
        else answer
            Note right of S: validate:<br/>normalize_response
            alt invalid, or first empty answer
                S->>M: "Rejected: reason"
            else valid
                Note right of S: write answer.json,<br/>end session
            end
        end
    end
    Note right of S: turn cap: abort,<br/>no answer.json

    opt 1800 s wall clock
        R->>S: docker kill
    end
    S-->>R: container exits
    Note over R,S: re-validate answer.json
    alt valid and non-empty
        Note over R,S: use agent answer
    else missing, invalid or empty
        Note over R,S: leave empty,<br/>or use --fallback
    end
